hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19111","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Ata, meaning Ibn al-Saib, from a man of Bakr ibn Wail, from his maternal uncle, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I take tithes from my people? He said: Tithes are only upon the Jews and the Christians, and there are no tithes upon Islam."
